From: liujixings <liujixings@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: ppe: keep offload setup when flow stats are unsupported

Not every NPU firmware variant implements the PPE flow stats mailbox
command. On the EN7581 + MT7996 firmware the NPU completes the HWNAT
init handshake (PPE_FLOW_CFG is programmed) but never answers
PPE_FUNC_SET_WAIT_FLOW_STATS_SETUP, so airoha_npu_ppe_stats_setup()
returns -ETIMEDOUT and airoha_ppe_offload_setup() bails out through
error_npu_put.

After that eth->npu stays NULL, airoha_ppe_hw_init() is never run (the
table base register keeps reading zero) and airoha_ppe_foe_entry_commit()
rejects every entry with -ENODEV, so neither routed nor L2B bridged
traffic can ever be offloaded.

Flow stats are an optional accounting feature: the debugfs status already
reports them as "unavailable" when the NPU stats window is not mapped.
Treat a stats setup failure as non fatal, skip the stats reset and the
stats readout while npu->stats is NULL, and let the rest of the PPE
offload setup complete.

Keeping the offload setup alive is not enough on its own: the per-entry
stats update rewrites IB2 so every accelerated flow is diverted to PSE
port 6 (CDM3/QDMA2_HWF) for the NPU to account it. Without a mapped stats
window nothing ever drains that queue, so it fills up until the PSE
shared buffer is exhausted and the whole switch stops forwarding. Skip
the diversion as well while npu->stats is NULL and leave the real egress
in place.

Signed-off-by: liujixings <liujixings@outlook.com>
Signed-off-by: naoki66 <naoki66@qq.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ppe.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ppe.c
@@ -723,6 +723,9 @@ static void airoha_ppe_foe_flow_stat_entry_reset(struct airoha_ppe *ppe,
 						 struct airoha_npu *npu,
 						 int index)
 {
+	if (!npu->stats)
+		return;
+
 	memset_io(&npu->stats[index], 0, sizeof(*npu->stats));
 	memset(&ppe->foe_stats[index], 0, sizeof(*ppe->foe_stats));
 }
@@ -846,6 +849,13 @@ static void airoha_ppe_foe_flow_stats_update(struct airoha_ppe *ppe,
 	if (airoha_is_7581(ppe->eth) && type == PPE_PKT_TYPE_BRIDGE)
 		return;
 
+	/* Flow accounting diverts every accelerated flow to CDM3 for the
+	 * NPU to consume; without a mapped stats window those frames are
+	 * neither accounted nor released, so keep the real egress here.
+	 */
+	if (!npu->stats)
+		return;
+
 	ppe_num_stats_entries = airoha_ppe_get_total_num_stats_entries(ppe);
 	if (ppe_num_stats_entries < 0)
 		return;
@@ -1947,7 +1950,7 @@ void airoha_ppe_foe_entry_get_stats(struct airoha_ppe *ppe, u32 hash,
 	rcu_read_lock();
 
 	npu = rcu_dereference(eth->npu);
-	if (npu) {
+	if (npu && npu->stats) {
 		u64 packets = ppe->foe_stats[index].packets;
 		u64 bytes = ppe->foe_stats[index].bytes;
 		struct airoha_foe_stats npu_stats;
@@ -2078,12 +2081,16 @@ static int airoha_ppe_offload_setup(struct airoha_eth *eth)
 	ppe_num_stats_entries = airoha_ppe_get_total_num_stats_entries(ppe);
 	if (ppe_num_stats_entries > 0) {
 		err = npu->ops.ppe_init_stats(npu, ppe->foe_stats_dma,
 					      ppe_num_stats_entries);
-		if (err)
-			goto error_npu_put;
+		if (err) {
+			dev_warn(eth->dev,
+				 "PPE flow stats unavailable: %d\n", err);
+			err = 0;
+		}
 	}
 
 	airoha_ppe_hw_init(ppe);
-	airoha_ppe_foe_flow_stats_reset(ppe, npu);
+	if (npu->stats)
+		airoha_ppe_foe_flow_stats_reset(ppe, npu);
 
 	rcu_assign_pointer(eth->npu, npu);
